fans of the marvel cinematic universe  love to dig through their favorite  movies for easter eggs and references  but some hidden secrets are harder to  find than others here are a few deep cut  easter eggs that took audiences multiple  years to discover  as the very first film in the marvel  cinematic universe iron man has a lot of  differences from the dozens of  expansions sequels and spin-offs that  followed it there's references to real  world conflicts no team-up action and  wait wait a second that's not don  cheadle one thing the mega franchise has  had since the very beginning however is  plenty of easter eggs and hidden  references to reward the most perceptive  fans the hidden details in iron man are  many but that doesn't mean they were all  easy to find in fact one particular  easter egg took fans a good decade to  discover tony stark's final adversary in  iron man is obadiah stain his former  mentor and the manager of stark  industries he starts out as a fairly  jovial presence propelled by that  trademark jeff bridges charisma that  even shines through stains immaculate  suits and chrome dome but there's a  sinister reality underneath in fact  stain was actually the one who planned  tony's kidnapping at the hands of the  mysterious ten rings organization in an  attempt to take the ceo position for  himself in the film's explosive climax  stain ends up donning the iron monger  suit and giving tony his first taste of  super villain combat in 2018 reddit user  hello to horse noticed that stain  actually foreshadows his true intentions  around an hour into the movie simply by  sitting behind a grand piano and playing  a peppy little tune while the scene  might look unassuming the man behind the  composition stain is playing is actually  antonio salieri an 18th century composer  who is depicted as the killer of  wolfgang amadeus mozart in the 1984 best  picture winning film amadeus while  there's no actual historical evidence  that salieri killed mozart in real life  the version of the composition played by  f murray abraham does mirror stains arc  in iron man eerily well after all both  stane and salieri are older less  brilliant talents who envy the prestige  of younger more celebrated geniuses to  the point that they start plotting their  respective downfalls  the first guardians of the galaxy is a  treasure trove of hidden references many  of which director james gunn has long  refused to point out not even to chris  pratt and other stars of his own film  although the movie came out in 2014  there may still be secrets just waiting  to be discovered as gunn has teased for  years that a massive discovery has gone  unnoticed for some time in april 2020  however the director did admit that a  large part of the final major guardians  of the galaxy easter egg had been  discovered some think that it might hint  that peter quill's mother meredith  played by laura haddock is actually a  cosmic force known as eternity that  embodies the universe itself the jury is  still out on whether or not that's  actually the case but fans have  certainly received their money's worth  of easter eggs from the blockbuster  ensemble comedy in 2018 four whole years  after the film's release gunn confirmed  a hitherto undiscovered easter egg in  which stan lee's cameo scene subtly  features lee's famous catchphrase  excelsior written in the skrull language  as recently as february 2021 the  director took to twitter to shoot down a  theory that an image of peter's father  ego was hiding in meredith's brain scans  and casually revealed that the brain  scans originally contained yet another  easter egg which may or may not actually  be in the final cut and that's not even  counting guardians of the galaxy vol 2  which has its own host of secrets for  inquisitive fans to uncover after all  these years i've found you  february 2nd 2018 was a good day for dr  strange director scott derrickson an  eagle-eyed fan had finally managed to  spot one of his favorite easter eggs  that he had hidden in the film as he  retweeted the discovery derekson  commented i've waited two years for  somebody to notice this twitter user tim  d lyden was the first to point out the  easter egg which reveals that one of the  most dramatic events in the movie the  car accident in which doctor strange  severely injures his hands happens on a  very particular date as dr strange  decides which of his expensive  timepieces to wear to the conference he  would end up crashing on route to a  quick glance at his watch face reveals  the date to be february 2nd a holiday  known as groundhog day while groundhog  day is a very real holiday in which a  rodent in pennsylvania predicts the  weather for the upcoming season it's  also the name of the legendary 1993 time  loop comedy starring the equally  legendary bill murray as a weatherman  sent to poxytoni to cover the annual  festivities murray's character phil  connors finds himself reliving groundhog  day over and over again doomed to spend  eternity reliving february 2nd unless he  can somehow find a way out the reference  is more than just an allusion to the  comedy classic it's also a subtle hint  at the good doctor's future after all  doctor strange eventually wins his  seemingly hopeless face-off against the  mighty dormammu by trapping the powerful  villain in a groundhog day style time  loop dooming it to live their  confrontation over and over again until  it becomes frustrated and gives up  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite marvel movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

